Hi,

My name is Jaci and I'm a student at ANU. I'm currently analysing data using latent profile analysis and am using the tidyLPA package in conjunction with mclust to do so. I was hoping to get some help about conducting a 3-step LPA.  (1) I have 3 continuous variables from which I would like to predict latent profiles. I would additionally like to (2) use predictor variables to create latent class probabilities for the most likely latent class membership, as well as (3) using these latent profiles as a predictor of distal outcomes.

Unfortunately I haven't been able to find any syntax which enables me to conduct steps 2 and 3 in r and I was wondering whether this is possible with the mclust/tidy package?

Many thanks in advance for any help.

Jaci Swinton

